## Identify $a$, $b$ and $c$
3x^2 - 6x - 8 &= 0
Here $a = 3$, $b = -6$ and $c = -8$. It does not factorise, so use the quadratic formula.
## Substitute into the formula
x &= \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}
&= \frac{-(-6) \pm \sqrt{(-6)^2 - 4(3)(-8)}}{2(3)}
&= \frac{6 \pm \sqrt{36 + 96}}{6}
&= \frac{6 \pm \sqrt{132}}{6}
## Find the plus root
x &= \frac{6 + \sqrt{132}}{6}
&\approx 2.9148
&\approx 2.9
## Find the minus root
x &= \frac{6 - \sqrt{132}}{6}
&\approx -0.9148
&\approx -0.9
ANSWER: x = 2.9 \text{ or } x = -0.9

## Set P(x) equal to 8350
275x - x^2 - 2000 &= 8350
0 &= x^2 - 275x + 2000 + 8350
0 &= x^2 - 275x + 10350
## Solve with the quadratic formula (a = 1, b = -275, c = 10350)
x &= \frac{275 \pm \sqrt{(-275)^2 - 4(1)(10350)}}{2}
x &= \frac{275 \pm \sqrt{75625 - 41400}}{2}
x &= \frac{275 \pm \sqrt{34225}}{2}
x &= \frac{275 \pm 185}{2}
x &= 230 \text{ or } x = 45
## Reject the value that is too big
The company can sell at most 200 km a week, so $x = 230$ is not possible.
x &= 45
ANSWER: x = 45\text{ km}

## Substitute M = 72.5 and h = 1.6
P &= \frac{72.5}{1.6^3}
&= \frac{72.5}{4.096}
&= 17.70\ldots
&\approx 17.7
ANSWER: P = 17.7

## Multiply both sides by h cubed
P &= \frac{M}{h^3}
Ph^3 &= M
## Divide both sides by P
h^3 &= \frac{M}{P}
## Take the cube root of both sides
h &= \sqrt[3]{\frac{M}{P}}
ANSWER: h = \sqrt[3]{\frac{M}{P}}

## Substitute M = 67.5 and P = 13
h &= \sqrt[3]{\frac{67.5}{13}}
&= \sqrt[3]{5.1923\ldots}
&= 1.7316\ldots
&\approx 1.73
ANSWER: h = 1.73\text{ m}
